{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966789,"nonce":"YbAYnK/r8tdaue6mGQW04Tr4koY=","title":"EventRouter::set_event_callback in windowed.rs Input arm uses a raw pointer to a","message":"The primary-window Input arm in `crates/blinc_app/src/windowed.rs` (around line 3626) sets an event callback that holds a raw pointer to a stack-local `pending_events: Vec\u003cPendingEvent\u003e`:\n\n```rust\nlet mut pending_events: Vec\u003cPendingEvent\u003e = Vec::new();\nrouter.set_event_callback({\n    let events = \u0026mut pending_events as *mut Vec\u003cPendingEvent\u003e;\n    move |node, event_type| {\n        unsafe { (*events).push(PendingEvent { ... }); }\n    }\n});\n```\n\nThe callback is meant to be cleared by the matching `router.clear_event_callback()` at the end of the same scope. The trap: any `return ControlFlow::Continue` between the set and the clear leaves the callback installed on the router with a now-dangling raw pointer. The next event that broadcasts through `emit_event` (notably `on_window_resize` from a `Resized` event) fires the stale callback, which writes into freed stack memory. The corrupted Vec header surfaces as a \"capacity overflow\" panic deep inside `RawVec::grow_one` — the actual UAF is invisible.\n\n**Symptom:** Resize the window after a mouse move that took the cursor-inside-last-leaf fast path → `thread 'main' panicked at raw_vec/mod.rs:28:5: capacity overflow` with `\u003cEventRouter\u003e::on_window_resize` → `broadcast_event` → `emit_event` → `\u003crun_desktop::closure#8::closure#16\u003e` (the raw-ptr push) → `RawVec::grow_one` in the stack.\n\n**Fix as of 2026-05-19:** Every early-return path between the set and the intended clear must call `router.clear_event_callback()` first. There are four such paths in `windowed.rs` (the three Mouse-Moved fast-path returns plus the `Key::Back` system-back-button case). Future early returns added in this region must also clear.\n\n**Why: How to apply:** when reviewing changes that add early returns inside the Input arm (between `set_event_callback` at ~3626 and `clear_event_callback` at ~4330), verify the callback is cleared first. The robust long-term fix is to replace the raw pointer with `Rc\u003cRefCell\u003cVec\u003cPendingEvent\u003e\u003e\u003e` — a dangling clone is then harmless (writes to a leaked-but-valid Vec instead of UB) and the per-return cleanup is no longer required. Hasn't been done because the push/iterate sites would need `borrow_mut()` everywhere (~15 call sites).","files":null}]}